From afeceea2657fe2f57c51461dbd5a3d9bfc30b76b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:42:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/52] ppc32: table switch without the 64-bit index
 zero-extension

G5 parade #11 of the 12.4 port, the first TurboFan JIT codegen item:
d8-smoke.js reached turbofan-hot and a concurrent optimization job
died in the code generator's opcode switch:

  # Fatal error in , line 0
  # unreachable code
  ... CodeGenerator::AssembleArchInstruction + 51064
  ... PipelineCompilationJob::ExecuteJobImpl /
      OptimizingCompileDispatcher::CompileTask::Run

No opcode in the message, so the culprit was derived statically
(scratchpad cgaudit.py, now node/cgaudit.py): every kPPC_/kArch opcode
the instruction selector emits from a ppc32-live region, checked
against the code generator's cases under the same guard view.  One
JS-reachable hit: VisitSwitch's jump-table path emits
kPPC_Uint32ToUint64 ("Zero extend, because we use it as 64-bit index
into the jump table", added upstream after 9.4), and that opcode's
code-generator case is PPC64-only, so on ppc32 it falls to the
switch's default: UNREACHABLE().  The smoke's murmur3 has a three-case
switch (values 1..3): table cost 4+3 + 3*3 = 16 <= lookup cost 3+6 +
3*3 = 18, so V8 picks the jump table, and murmur3 is the hottest
function in the loop.  Jump tables are enabled for TURBOFAN and
WASM_FUNCTION code kinds only, which is why the builtins in mksnapshot
never met this and why the snapshot is unchanged by the fix.

Guard the zero-extension PPC64-only.  On ppc32 the 32-bit index
register is the jump-table index as it is: AssembleArchTableSwitch
compares with CmpU64, shifts with ShiftLeftU64 and loads with LoadU64,
all of which are pointer-size-lowered (slwi / lwz) by patch 0004 - the
same shape 9.4 ran on the G5 (its VisitSwitch had no extension).

Audit remainder (all runtime-dead on ppc32): kPPC_Add64 is the is64
arm of turboshaft's overflow-compare fusion, kPPC_Mul64/kPPC_Cmp64 live
in EmitInt64MulWithOverflow (Int64-only callers), kPPC_ByteRev64 in
VisitWord64ReverseBytes (Word64 nodes do not exist in 32-bit graphs),
the S128 lane/splat opcodes are macro-listed in the code generator
(literal-scan blind spot) and SIMD is rejected.  A companion pass over
live code-generator cases that call macro-assembler helpers whose ppc32
body is UNREACHABLE finds only SIMD (F64x2*, I64x2Mul) and sandbox
(Load/StoreSandboxedPointerField, StoreIndirectPointerField) sites,
none of which the ppc32 selector emits.
---
 v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
index 1df5def..a185543 100644
--- a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
@@ -2817,10 +2817,15 @@ void InstructionSelectorT<Adapter>::VisitSwitch(node_t node,
       Emit(kPPC_Sub, index_operand, value_operand,
            g.TempImmediate(sw.min_value()));
       }
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
       // Zero extend, because we use it as 64-bit index into the jump table.
       InstructionOperand index_operand_zero_ext = g.TempRegister();
       Emit(kPPC_Uint32ToUint64, index_operand_zero_ext, index_operand);
       index_operand = index_operand_zero_ext;
+#endif
+      // On ppc32 the 32-bit index register is the jump-table index as it is
+      // (AssembleArchTableSwitch shifts and loads at pointer size), and
+      // kPPC_Uint32ToUint64 has no 32-bit code-generator case.
       // Generate a table lookup.
       return EmitTableSwitch(sw, index_operand);
   }
